# The ark: the generation ship, after the war on board. Built by
# `go run ./tools/mapgen -map ark`; this file is the level, and map.bin,
# map.json and the atlas beside them are what it compiles to.
#
# A cone standing on its point. The drive is in the tip, the decks are in the
# wide part of the cone, and the drum and the ice dome on top are the heavy end:
# the reaction mass and the shield. "Down" is towards the tip whatever the ship
# is doing - thrust pushes the floor up at you from the engine side, and the
# end-over-end tumble it coasted on for centuries throws you away from the
# heavy drum, which is the same way. So the decks are flat and gravity is the
# engine's own -Y. The sky does not turn: two weeks out, the drive is burning.
#
#   y 94-104   ice dome        water ice: dust and radiation shield
#   y 78-94    drum R22        tanks, the AI core in the middle, 8 booms
#   y 75-77    D6 command      vented by the AI                    vacuum
#   y 72-74    D5 farm         blown open, frozen                  vacuum
#   y 69-71    D4 elite        window band, burnt out              air
#   y 66-68    D3 medical      gene vault, the lab you wake in     air
#   y 63-65    D2 crew         bunks, mess, airlock east (+z)      air
#   y 60-62    D1 sump         life support, water, airlock west   air
#   y 22-59    lower cone      tanks round the spine shaft         vacuum
#   y  0-21    drive           reactor, shadow shield, the bell
#
# A voxel is two metres (the player is 0.875 of one). The hull's radius is
# r(y) = 3 + (y-8)*15/70 all the way from the tip at y=8 to the drum at y=78;
# every radius below that says "r(y)" is that line read at that height, and
# changing the cone means changing all of them.
#
# Doors, ladders and everything else that is a thing rather than a wall are
# not placed yet. The spine is the one way between decks: a ladder goes up it.

size 112 112 112
sky full
fog 200 900
ambient 0.55 0.60 0.75 0.30
ceiling 4 5 10
floor 4 5 10
music maintenance

# D3, beside the spine door, facing it.
spawn 63.5 67 56.5 dir=-1,0

# Air on D1-D4 and nowhere else: out to the hull's outside, r(y), from D1's
# floor to D4's ceiling. Out to the outside rather than the inside so the glass,
# which stands in the wall, is not a step into vacuum; an airlock's chamber is
# past the hull, so it is still vacuum by the time you stand in it.
pressure 56.5 56.5 14.36 61 72 16.71

# --------------------------------------------------------------- textures ---
tex hull     Space/_original/METAL_1A.PNG
tex hull2    Space/_original/PANEL_4A.PNG
tex drum     Space/_original/CLADDING_1B.PNG
tex ice      ark/ice.png glow
tex floor    Space/_original/FLOOR_1A.PNG
tex ceil     Space/_original/PANEL_1A.PNG
tex strip    Space/_original/LIGHT_3A.PNG glow
tex grate    Space/_original/GRID_1A.PNG
tex girder   Space/_original/SUPPORT_1A.PNG
tex fin      Space/_original/CORRUGAT_1A.PNG
tex scorch   shock/087_industrial_tiles.png
tex warn     Space/_original/WARN_1A.PNG
tex steel    Space/_original/STEEL_1A.PNG
tex reactor  shock/002_magnetic_containment_system.png
tex flame    shock/188_incandescent_light.png glow
tex crop     shock/203_grass.png
tex rack     shock/209_overgrown_panel.png
tex server   shock/122_tech_rack.png
tex tank     Space/_original/METAL_1C.PNG

# -------------------------------------------------------------- materials ---
# wall, floor, ceiling
block hull    hull
block habhull hull2 floor ceil
block deck    ceil floor ceil
block drum    drum
block ice     ice
block strip   strip hull2 hull2
block spine   grate
block girder  girder
block fin     fin
block scorch  scorch
block lock    warn steel steel
block steel   steel
block reactor reactor
block throat  flame
block crop    rack crop
block console server steel
block tank    tank

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- dome ---
# First, because a cap is a sphere with the rest cut away and the cut takes the
# whole band under it: a radius-30 ball whose top is 10 voxels above the drum
# and whose rim meets the drum's edge at y=94.
ball ice 56 73.6 56 30
clear 0 0 0 111 94 111

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ drive ---
# The bell opens downwards from the throat, which is lit: the drive is on.
cone steel 56 56 7 0 3 7 shell=1
cone throat 56 56 2 7 2 7
# The tip is solid reactor, the hull skin goes over it, and the shadow shield
# above it is what the decks are standing behind.
cone reactor 56 56 3 8 5.14 18
cone steel 56 56 5 19 5 21

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- hull ---
cone hull 56 56 3 8 18 78 shell=1.5
# The decks' own band of it, lighter, from D1's floor to the drum.
cone habhull 56 56 14.14 60 18 78 shell=1.5

# Three tanks round the spine in the lower cone, all of it reaction mass.
cone tank 61.5 56 2.5 40 2.5 57
cone tank 53.25 60.76 2.5 40 2.5 57
cone tank 53.25 51.24 2.5 40 2.5 57

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- drum ---
# Wider than the cone, so the decks' roof is the middle of its floor and the
# ledge round it is drum.
cone drum 56 56 22 78 22 78
cone drum 56 56 22 79 22 94 shell=1.5
cone drum 56 56 22 94 22 94
# The AI core: a vault of racks on the spine's axis, at the ship's heart.
cone console 56 56 5 79 5 91 shell=1
cone console 56 56 5 91 5 91
# Six tanks round it, one every sixty degrees from thirty.
ball tank 67.26 86 62.5 4
ball tank 56 86 69 4
ball tank 44.74 86 62.5 4
ball tank 44.74 86 49.5 4
ball tank 56 86 43 4
ball tank 67.26 86 49.5 4

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ decks ---
# A floor every three voxels, each out to r(y) so it meets the hull; the top
# one is the roof, which is the middle of the drum's floor.
cone deck 56 56 14.14 60 14.14 60
cone deck 56 56 14.79 63 14.79 63
cone deck 56 56 15.43 66 15.43 66
cone deck 56 56 16.07 69 16.07 69
cone deck 56 56 16.71 72 16.71 72
cone deck 56 56 17.36 75 17.36 75
cone deck 56 56 18 78 18 78

# A lit strip under the ceiling of D1-D3: the deck's own light indoors, and a
# band on the hull outside for each deck that still has power.
cone strip 56 56 14.57 62 14.57 62 shell=1.5
cone strip 56 56 15.21 65 15.21 65 shell=1.5
cone strip 56 56 15.86 68 15.86 68 shell=1.5

# D4's promenade: floor to ceiling glass the whole way round. The hull is
# carved out of the band first, then glazed; the glass ring sits inside the
# carved one, so what is left either side of it is air.
cone air 56 56 16.29 70 16.5 71 shell=1.5
glass 56 56 16 15 70
glass 56 56 16 15 71

# D5, the farm: a disc of growing racks with walkways cut across it, a clear
# lane round the wall and round the spine.
cone crop 56 56 13 73 13 73
clear 51 73 44 61 73 44
clear 47 73 47 65 73 47
clear 45 73 50 67 73 50
clear 44 73 53 68 73 53
clear 44 73 59 68 73 59
clear 45 73 62 67 73 62
clear 47 73 65 65 73 65
clear 51 73 68 61 73 68
clear 52 73 52 60 73 60

# D6, the bridge: a ring of consoles round the spine, two aisles through it.
cone console 56 56 6 76 6 76 shell=1
clear 55 76 48 57 76 64
clear 48 76 55 64 76 57

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ spine ---
# The maintenance shaft from the shadow shield to the core: a grate tube with
# a 3x3 well inside it, through every floor. A door out of it on each deck,
# one voxel tall so a slide door fits with the deck above as its lintel.
cone spine 56 56 2.5 22 2.5 78 shell=1
cone air 56 56 1.45 22 1.45 78
clear 58 61 56 58 61 56
clear 58 64 56 58 64 56
clear 58 67 56 58 67 56
clear 58 70 56 58 70 56
clear 58 73 56 58 73 56
clear 58 76 56 58 76 56

# --------------------------------------------------------------- airlocks ---
# A box on the hull, a chamber in it, a one-voxel passage through both. The
# door cells are marked for when doors go in; each has lock above it.
# D2, east (+z): inner door z=71, outer door z=76.
fill lock 54 63 70 58 66 77
clear 55 64 72 57 65 75
clear 56 64 69 56 64 77
# D1, west (-x): inner door x=42, outer door x=35.
fill lock 34 60 54 42 63 58
clear 36 61 55 40 62 57
clear 34 61 56 43 61 56

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ booms ---
# Eight radiator booms round the drum at y=86, one every 45 degrees. Three
# survived: the sensor mast east, and the two radiators north-west and north.
# The other five are stubs, and what came off them is still drifting.
#
# east (+x): the long-range sensor mast, which heard the planet first.
beam girder 77 86 56 100 86 56 r=1
ball steel 105 86 56 5 shell=1
clear 104 76 46 111 96 66
# north-west: radiator, a corrugated fin above and below the boom.
beam girder 41.15 86 70.85 23.47 86 88.53 r=1
beam fin 38.32 83 73.68 24.18 83 87.82 r=0.5
beam fin 38.32 84 73.68 24.18 84 87.82 r=0.5
beam fin 38.32 85 73.68 24.18 85 87.82 r=0.5
beam fin 38.32 87 73.68 24.18 87 87.82 r=0.5
beam fin 38.32 88 73.68 24.18 88 87.82 r=0.5
beam fin 38.32 89 73.68 24.18 89 87.82 r=0.5
# north (-z): radiator.
fill fin 56 83 11 56 89 31
beam girder 56 86 35 56 86 10 r=1
# The stubs.
beam girder 70.85 86 70.85 77.21 86 77.21 r=1
beam girder 86 83 84 92 89 93 r=1
beam girder 56 86 77 56 86 82 r=1
beam girder 35 86 56 22 86 56 r=1
beam girder 41.15 86 41.15 36.2 86 36.2 r=1
beam girder 70.85 86 41.15 78.63 86 33.37 r=1

# ----------------------------------------------------------------- damage ---
# Last, so every hole goes through whatever was built where it landed.
#
# The farm, blown open from outside the hull: the war stopped being about who
# ran the ship when someone decided the other side could starve. It takes the
# floor of D6 with it, so the two vented decks are one hole.
# Two holes side by side, high enough that the ragged edge stops short of D4's
# floor; D4's ceiling is laid again under them, because D4 still holds air.
blast 72 75 53 3.5 seed=1 scorch=scorch debris=8
blast 72 75 59 3.5 seed=21 scorch=scorch debris=8
cone deck 56 56 16.71 72 16.71 72
# The way into the core, blown through the top of the spine by the people who
# came to switch the AI off. The AI vented D6 to stop them.
blast 56 78 56 2.5 seed=2 scorch=scorch
# D6's emergency vents, opened: the hull cut through either side of the bridge.
clear 54 76 38 58 77 41
clear 54 76 71 58 77 74
# The drum, holed twice, one tank torn open behind the bigger hole.
blast 75 86 67 4.5 seed=3 scorch=scorch debris=10
blast 37 82 45 3.5 seed=4 scorch=scorch debris=8
# The lower cone, a tank showing through.
blast 46 44 52 4 seed=5 scorch=scorch debris=8
# A crater in the ice.
blast 64 101 50 3 seed=6 scorch=ice debris=6
# Where the five booms broke.
blast 77.21 86 77.21 2 seed=11 scorch=scorch debris=5
blast 56 86 82 2 seed=12 scorch=scorch debris=4
blast 22 86 56 2.2 seed=14 scorch=scorch debris=6
blast 36.2 86 36.2 2 seed=15 scorch=scorch debris=4
blast 78.63 86 33.37 2 seed=17 scorch=scorch debris=5
# D4 burnt out from the inside: scorch on floor and ceiling, nothing opened.
blast 50 70.5 60 0.6 seed=7 scorch=scorch
blast 62 70.5 50 0.6 seed=8 scorch=scorch
blast 60 70.5 64 0.6 seed=9 scorch=scorch

